invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser_ee.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the parser reads a server_certificate_type even when the
  ClientHello offered no certificate type, so a response to a request
  that never went out is judged on its contents instead of refused.
  RFC 9846 §4.3 answers an unrequested extension with
  unsupported_extension, and the alert here becomes illegal_parameter,
  which names the wrong fault. bin/handshake_strict_webpki's no-offer
  rows object.

--- old
    if (ext == EXT_SERVER_CERTIFICATE_TYPE && out->cert_types_offered != 0) {
--- new
    if (ext == EXT_SERVER_CERTIFICATE_TYPE) {
